# Building and testing

This is a standalone Go implementation. It uses only the Go standard library;
there are no modules to fetch and no runtime dependencies on another command.
A Go 1.21 or newer toolchain is sufficient.

```sh
./compile.sh       # writes ./executable
go test ./...      # runs the source-level regression tests
```

The executable reads consecutive JSON objects from standard input. Its CLI and
report formats are described in the bundled README.

## Implementation notes

* Input is decoded completely before output is written. An invalid record
  prevents a partially rendered report. Errors are logged by the CLI.
* Filtering preserves order and duplicates. Root modules are omitted; the
  direct/update filters inspect the original module record.
* A replacement supplies the displayed current version, update, and timestamp
  comparison, but not the module name or directness. Replacements are followed
  one level only. CI status is based on updates in the selected effective records.
* The independent table renderer supports bordered and Markdown output. It
  centers headers, right-aligns numeric values, and computes display widths for
  terminal grapheme clusters. Word wrapping minimizes squared unused space,
  excluding the final line, and allows words longer than the normal width limit.
* Terminal character-width classes and locale handling are self-contained.
  Neither table formatting nor Unicode handling requires an external library.

Build outputs and temporary behavioral test artifacts are ignored by Git.
EOF
